      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "eps/teaser",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 654
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\end{center}",
      "n_tokens_est": 5,
      "pos_start_est": 657
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\vspace",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 662
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "-1.2em",
      "n_tokens_est": 4,
      "pos_start_est": 664
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\caption",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 668
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "Training error (left) and test error (right) on CIFAR-10 with 20-layer and 56-layer ",
      "n_tokens_est": 23,
      "pos_start_est": 670
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "``",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 693
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "plain",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 695
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "''",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 696
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " networks. The deeper network has higher training error, and thus test error. Similar phenomena on ImageNet is presented in Fig.",
      "n_tokens_est": 24,
      "pos_start_est": 698
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "~",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 722
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\ref",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 723
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "fig:imagenet",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 725
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ".",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 728
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "fig:teaser",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 729
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\vspace",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 732
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "-1em",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 734
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\end{figure}",
      "n_tokens_est": 5,
      "pos_start_est": 736
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " When deeper networks are able to start converging, a ",
      "n_tokens_est": 10,
      "pos_start_est": 741
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\emph",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 751
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "degradation",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 753
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " problem has been exposed: with the network depth increasing, accuracy gets saturated (which might be unsurprising) and then degrades rapidly. Unexpectedly, such degradation is ",
      "n_tokens_est": 30,
      "pos_start_est": 754
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\emph",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 784
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "not caused by overfitting",
      "n_tokens_est": 4,
      "pos_start_est": 786
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ", and adding more layers to a suitably deep model leads to ",
      "n_tokens_est": 12,
      "pos_start_est": 790
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\emph",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 802
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "higher training error",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 804
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ", as reported in ",
      "n_tokens_est": 4,
      "pos_start_est": 807
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\cite",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 811
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "He2015a, Srivastava2015",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 813
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " and thoroughly verified by our experiments. Fig.",
      "n_tokens_est": 9,
      "pos_start_est": 816
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "~",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 825
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\ref",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 826
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "fig:teaser",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 828
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " shows a typical example. The degradation (of training accuracy) indicates that not all systems are similarly easy to optimize. Let us consider a shallower architecture and its deeper counterpart that adds more layers onto it. There exists a solution ",
      "n_tokens_est": 44,
      "pos_start_est": 831
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\emph",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 875
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "by construction",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 877
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " to the deeper model: the added layers are ",
      "n_tokens_est": 9,
      "pos_start_est": 879
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\emph",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 888
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "identity",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 890
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " mapping, and the other layers are copied from the learned shallower model. The existence of this constructed solution indicates that a deeper model should produce no higher training error than its shallower counterpart. But experiments show that our current solvers on hand are unable to find solutions that are comparably good or better than the constructed solution (or unable to do so in feasible time). In this paper, we address the degradation problem by introducing a ",
      "n_tokens_est": 83,
      "pos_start_est": 891
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\emph",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 974
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "deep residual learning",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 976
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " framework. Instead of hoping each few stacked layers directly fit a desired underlying mapping, we explicitly let these layers fit a residual mapping. Formally, denoting the desired underlying mapping as ",
      "n_tokens_est": 34,
      "pos_start_est": 979
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "$\\mathcal{H}(\\ve{x})$",
      "n_tokens_est": 14,
      "pos_start_est": 1013
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ", we let the stacked nonlinear layers fit another mapping of ",
      "n_tokens_est": 11,
      "pos_start_est": 1027
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "$\\mathcal{F}(\\ve{x}):=\\mathcal{H}(\\ve{x})-\\ve{x}$",
      "n_tokens_est": 34,
      "pos_start_est": 1038
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ". The original mapping is recast into ",
      "n_tokens_est": 7,
      "pos_start_est": 1072
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "$\\mathcal{F}(\\ve{x})+\\ve{x}$",
      "n_tokens_est": 20,
      "pos_start_est": 1079
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ". We hypothesize that it is easier to optimize the residual mapping than to optimize the original, unreferenced mapping. To the extreme, if an identity mapping were optimal, it would be easier to push the residual to zero than to fit an identity mapping by a stack of nonlinear layers. The formulation of ",
      "n_tokens_est": 58,
      "pos_start_est": 1099
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "$\\mathcal{F}(\\ve{x})+\\ve{x}$",
      "n_tokens_est": 20,
      "pos_start_est": 1157
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " can be realized by feedforward neural networks with ",
      "n_tokens_est": 8,
      "pos_start_est": 1177
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "``",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1185
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "shortcut connections",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1187
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "''",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1189
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " (Fig.",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 1191
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "~",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 1194
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\ref",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1195
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "fig:block",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 1197
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "). Shortcut connections ",
      "n_tokens_est": 4,
      "pos_start_est": 1200
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\cite",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1204
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "Bishop1995,Ripley1996,Venables1999",
      "n_tokens_est": 5,
      "pos_start_est": 1206
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " are those skipping one or more layers. In our case, the shortcut connections simply perform ",
      "n_tokens_est": 17,
      "pos_start_est": 1211
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\emph",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1228
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "identity",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 1230
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " mapping, and their outputs are added to the outputs of the stacked layers (Fig.",
      "n_tokens_est": 17,
      "pos_start_est": 1231
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "~",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 1248
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\ref",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1249
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "fig:block",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 1251
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "). Identity shortcut connections add neither extra parameter nor computational complexity. The entire network can still be trained end-to-end by SGD with backpropagation, and can be easily implemented using common libraries (",
      "n_tokens_est": 39,
      "pos_start_est": 1254
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\eg",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1293
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ", Caffe ",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1295
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\cite",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1297
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "Jia2014",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 1299
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": ") without modifying the solvers. ",
      "n_tokens_est": 6,
      "pos_start_est": 1300
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\begin{figure}",
      "n_tokens_est": 5,
      "pos_start_est": 1306
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\centering",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1311
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\hspace",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1313
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "48pt",
      "n_tokens_est": 1,
      "pos_start_est": 1315
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\includegraphics",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1316
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "width=0.9",
      "n_tokens_est": 5,
      "pos_start_est": 1318
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\linewidth",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1323
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "eps/block",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 1325
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\vspace",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1328
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "-.5em",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 1330
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\caption",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1333
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "Residual learning: a building block.",
      "n_tokens_est": 7,
      "pos_start_est": 1335
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "fig:block",
      "n_tokens_est": 3,
      "pos_start_est": 1342
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\vspace",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1345
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": "-1em",
      "n_tokens_est": 2,
      "pos_start_est": 1347
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "markup",
      "text": "\\end{figure}",
      "n_tokens_est": 5,
      "pos_start_est": 1349
    },
    {
      "node_id": 2,
      "seq_id": 1,
      "kind": "content",
      "text": " We present comprehensive experiments on ImageNet ",
